## A two sided view:  a view with a front and a back, showing one at a time
// Built into spell (epic `elemental-spell` Q71):  compiled once, into the core's `TwoSidedView`.
// A view made from it says what each side looks like, with `to draw its front:` and `to draw its back:`.
a "two sided view" is a view where:
	- it has parts "front" and "back"
	// which way it faces:  a new one starts face down
	- its "direction" is down or up
	- it "is face (direction)"
	- to turn it face up:
		set its direction to up
	- to turn it face down:
		set its direction to down
	- to turn it over:
		if it is face down
			turn it face up
		otherwise
			turn it face down
	// its front when it's face up, its back when it's face down
	- to draw it:
		if it is face down
			draw its back
		otherwise
			draw its front
